{
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": "CLIHub subagent model policy. THREE axes per dispatch: model (which model), effort (reasoning level), and the fallback chain. TWO LAYERS: this file (versioned, human-curated) + .opencode/model-policy.json (gitignored runtime selection). Resolution at dispatch: effective_preset = first override whose window contains now, else active_preset; take the role's ordered list, drop models whose exhausted_until is in the future, try in order. Availability failure (429/quota/billing/auth/not-found) -> mark exhausted_until = now + backoff, try next. Quality failure -> escalate to the next model in the same list. If on_exhaustion is block_and_ask and no acceptable model remains -> STOP and ask the user. Merge rule for the runtime file: the orchestrator owns exhaustedUntil and sessionLog; the sidebar owns activePreset and roleOverrides; each writer read-modify-writes only its own fields, atomically.",
  "_effort_note": "effort is a normalized level (off|low|medium|high|max) that the resolver maps onto the chosen model's supported `variants` (the lowest variant at or above the level, else the highest available; `off` means `none` when supported, otherwise no variant). A chain entry may override it as `model#variant`. Reasoning level consumes more tokens, so on a metered plan a high effort burns the quota faster; the exhaustion logic does not yet weight this.",
  "active_preset": "default",
  "display": {
    "_comment": "Display-only abbreviations for the model-policy panel and dialogs. The versioned policy owns them so the panel and the documentation cannot drift apart. Nothing here changes the resolution: the full model id is always what is resolved, logged and written. providers: the provider id prefix -> its short code. models: the model name (without the provider) -> its short form; only the vendor word is shortened, the version and the tier stay verbatim. variants: the reasoning effort -> one letter (M is max, m is medium, i is minimal, l is low). roles: the role name -> its code in the narrow role column. drop_free_suffix_for: providers whose model names end in '-free'; the suffix is redundant there because every model of those providers is a free one.",
